Summary: Feide Auto-Group Assignment Context & Current Implementation
I've completed a comprehensive exploration of your PHIS repository. Here's the specific context about the Feide automatic group assignment issue:

The Problem You Described
When Feide users create an account, they experience friction because:

Account is created via OpenID Connect callback
User needs to be assigned to the "Users" group to receive credentials
Currently: Assignment happens via a Python daemon that polls every 60 seconds
Result: Users see a blank page or no permissions for up to 60 seconds, requiring a refresh to see the interface
Current Implementation: Dual-System Approach
You have TWO mechanisms for auto-group assignment:

Mechanism 1: Java Patch (JIT - Just-In-Time) ✅ Modern Solution
File: tools/opensilex-patch-auto-groups.sh

This patches AccountDAO.java in the OpenSILEX source code to assign groups immediately when accounts are created:


// In AccountDAO.getByEmailOrCreate() method, after create(account):
URI defaultGroupUri = new URI("http://opensilex.org/groups/users");
URI defaultProfileUri = new URI("http://opensilex.org/profiles/default");

GroupDAO groupDAO = new GroupDAO(sparql, nosql);
GroupModel defaultGroup = groupDAO.get(defaultGroupUri);

GroupUserProfileModel userProfile = new GroupUserProfileModel();
userProfile.setUserURI(account.getUri());
userProfile.setProfileURI(defaultProfileUri);

defaultGroup.getUserProfiles().add(userProfile);
groupDAO.update(defaultGroup);
Location in source: Lines 46-87 in the patch file

Advantages:

✅ Zero latency - user gets credentials immediately on first login
✅ No daemon required - integrated into account creation logic
✅ No refresh needed - eliminates the friction you mentioned
